This is work in progress by Rob Speer - I'm leaving notes to myself for what to fill in.

!Proposed Definitions

;ko'a, ko'e, ko'i, ko'o, ko'u, fo'a, fo'e, fo'i, fo'o, fo'u: Assignable pro-sumti. The referent of each word can be assigned using ''goi''.

  i le nanmu goi ko'a cu klama le zarci i ko'a viska re nanmu
  ''A man goes to the market. He sees two men.''

;vo'a: The x1 of this bridi.
;vo'e: The x2 of this bridi.
;vo'i: The x3 of this bridi.
;vo'o: The x4 of this bridi.
;vo'u: The x5 of this bridi.

  i la risna noltruni'u cu zutse le vo'a nolstizu
  ''The Queen of Hearts sat on her throne.''

;ri: Repeats the previous sumti.
;ra: Repeats a recent, but usually not the previous, sumti.
;ru: Repeats an earlier sumti, to be determined from context.

;ti: This here - an object near the speaker.
;ta: That there - an object near the listener.
;tu: That yonder - an object far from the speaker and the listener.

!Proposed keywords
 ko'a  it-1
 ko'e  it-2
 ko'i  it-3
 ko'o  it-4
 ko'u  it-5
 fo'a  it-6
 fo'e  it-7
 fo'i  it-8
 fo'o  it-9
 fo'u  it-10
 vo'a  x1 it
 vo'e  x2 it
 vo'i  x3 it
 vo'o  x4 it
 vo'u  x5 it
 ri    last sumti
 ra    recent sumti
 ru    earlier sumti
 ti    this here
 ta    that there
 tu    that yonder

!Usage clarifications
The __vo'a__-series cmavo refer to the sumti of the ''outermost'' bridi of the sentence. (This was left unspecified in CLL, and decided by a significant majority of usage.)